„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙêForasmuch therefore as your treading is upon the poor, and ye take from him burdens of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink wine of them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate from their right.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNTherefore the prudent shall keep silence in that time; for it is an evil time.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsSeek good, and not evil, that ye may live: and so the LORD, the God of hosts, shall be with you, as ye have spoken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—Hate the evil, and love the good, and establish judgment in the gate: it may be that the LORD God of hosts will be gracious unto the remnant of Joseph.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙóTherefore the LORD, the God of hosts, the Lord, saith thus; Wailing shall be in all streets; and they shall say in all the highways, Alas! alas! and they shall call the husbandman to mourning, and such as are skilful of lamentation to wailing.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd in all vineyards shall be wailing: for I will pass through thee, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxWoe unto you that desire the day of the LORD! to what end is it for you? the day of the LORD is darkness, and not light.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…As if a man did flee from a lion, and a bear met him; or went into the house, and leaned his hand on the wall, and a serpent bit him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbShall not the day of the LORD be darkness, and not light? even very dark, and no brightness in it?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRI hate, I despise your feast days, and I will not smell in your solemn assemblies.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘Though ye offer me burnt offerings and your meat offerings, I will not accept them: neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat beasts.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Take thou away from me the noise of thy songs; for I will not hear the melody of thy viols.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJBut let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbHave ye offered unto me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, O house of Israel?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyBut ye have borne the tabernacle of your Moloch and Chiun your images, the star of your god, which ye made to yourselves.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpTherefore will I cause you to go into captivity beyond Damascus, saith the LORD, whose name is The God of hosts.¦layout ªlast_verse